				\begin{document}$$\:\text{Occurrence} \:\text{of}\:\text{EF}\:=\frac{\text{Number}\:\text{of}\:\text{colonies}\:\text{of}\:\text{species}}{\text{Total}\:\text{number}\:\text{of}\:\text{isolated}\:\text{colonies}}\times\:100$$\end{document}

Colonization frequency percentage (CF%) was utilized to compare the degrees of EF isolates between different plant tissues, calculated according to the method described by Suryanarayanan et al.71\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
